From: Jose Olivera <oliverajeo@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sdk_dpaa: add dpa_unregister_ipsec_fq_handler

Companion to the existing dpa_register_ipsec_fq_handler(). The
registration function, as added by the main ASK kernel patch, guards
against re-registration:

    if (cdx_get_ipsec_fq_hookfn) {
        printk("%s::hook already registered\n", __FUNCTION__);
        return -1;
    }
    cdx_get_ipsec_fq_hookfn = hookfn;

There is no symmetric clear path: passing NULL to the register function
is rejected by the same guard once a hook is already installed, and the
cdx_get_ipsec_fq_hookfn global is not exported, so ASK's cdx module
cannot null it out on module unload.

The practical consequence is that unloading cdx leaves sdk_dpaa holding
a function pointer into freed module memory. The next outbound IPsec
packet dereferences that pointer in the NULL-guarded
    if ((cdx_get_ipsec_fq_hookfn) && (sp) && (sp->len))
path of dpaa_eth_sg.c — use-after-free, likely an oops. A subsequent
modprobe of cdx is also blocked because the register function still
sees the stale non-NULL pointer and returns -1.

This patch adds an explicit deregister function that sets the hook back
to NULL and exports it. ASK's cdx/control_ipsec.c:ipsec_exit() calls
this in its normal cleanup path to make module unload/reload safe.

For the OpenWRT layerscape target, install this as
target/linux/layerscape/patches-6.12/960-nxp-ask-ipsec-fq-handler-unregister.patch
(or merge the two hunks into 951-nxp-ask.patch). This patch applies on
top of 951-nxp-ask.patch (which must already have introduced
dpa_register_ipsec_fq_handler and cdx_get_ipsec_fq_hookfn).

Signed-off-by: Jose Olivera <oliverajeo@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth_common.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth_common.h
@@ -100,6 +100,7 @@
 #if defined(CONFIG_INET_IPSEC_OFFLOAD) || defined(CONFIG_INET6_IPSEC_OFFLOAD)
 typedef struct qman_fq *(*cdx_get_ipsec_fq_hook_t)(u32 handle);
 int dpa_register_ipsec_fq_handler(cdx_get_ipsec_fq_hook_t hookfn);
+void dpa_unregister_ipsec_fq_handler(void);
 int dpaa_submit_inb_pkt_to_SEC(struct sk_buff *skb, uint16_t sagd);
  __hot void dpaa_submit_outb_pkt_to_SEC(struct sk_buff *skb, struct net_device *net_dev, struct dpa_bp *dpa_bp);

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth_sg.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_dpaa/dpaa_eth_sg.c
@@ -101,6 +101,12 @@

 EXPORT_SYMBOL(dpa_register_ipsec_fq_handler);

+void dpa_unregister_ipsec_fq_handler(void)
+{
+	cdx_get_ipsec_fq_hookfn = NULL;
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL(dpa_unregister_ipsec_fq_handler);
+
 #endif

 /* DMA map and add a page frag back into the bpool.
